Your task is to implement the link_roots operation for a Union-Find data structure, which performs the actual merging of two sets, and verify its correctness in Verus. This operation takes two distinct valid roots, $root_i$ and $root_j$, and merges their trees into a single set using the Union-by-Rank heuristic to maintain balance. The operation applies one of three cases: (1) Attach Smaller: If $rank[root_i] < rank[root_j]$, make $root_j$ the parent of $root_i$. (2) Attach Equal: If $rank[root_i] == rank[root_j]$, arbitrarily make $root_j$ the parent of $root_i$ and increment the rank of $root_j$ by 1. (3) Attach Larger: If $rank[root_j] < rank[root_i]$, make $root_i$ the parent of $root_j$.Specifically, you must prove the following: (1) Merged Sets: After the operation, the two input roots (and consequently all nodes in their respective trees) must share the same representative logical root. (2) Rank Invariant: The strict rank ordering property (where a parent's rank is strictly greater than its children's ranks) must be preserved for every node in the tree. This guarantees the tree structure remains a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) and ensures termination. (3) Frame Condition: The operation must only affect the logical sets associated with $root_i$ and $root_j$. The representatives for all other disjoint sets in the structure must remain unchanged.
----
     1	use vstd::prelude::*;
     2	
     3	verus! {
     4	    // Following is the block for necessary definitions
     5	    // <preamble>
     6	    pub struct UnionFind {
     7	        pub parent: Vec<usize>,
     8	        pub rank: Vec<usize>,
     9	    }
    10	
    11	    impl UnionFind {
    12	        pub open spec fn is_valid(&self) -> bool {
    13	            &&& self.parent.len() == self.rank.len()
    14	            &&& forall|i: usize| 0 <= i < self.parent.len() ==> {
    15	                let p = #[trigger] self.parent[i as int];
    16	                &&& p < self.parent.len()
    17	                &&& self.rank[i as int] < self.parent.len()
    18	                &&& (p != i ==> self.rank[i as int] < self.rank[p as int])
    19	            }
    20	        }
    21	
    22	        pub open spec fn measure(&self, i: usize) -> usize {
    23	            if i < self.rank.len() && self.rank[i as int] < self.parent.len() {
    24	                 (self.parent.len() - self.rank[i as int]) as usize
    25	            } else {
    26	                 0
    27	            }
    28	        }
    29	
    30	        pub open spec fn spec_find(&self, i: usize) -> usize 
    31	            decreases self.measure(i)
    32	        {
    33	            if i < self.parent.len() && i < self.rank.len() && self.rank[i as int] < self.parent.len() {
    34	                let p = self.parent[i as int];
    35	                if p != i && p < self.rank.len() && self.rank[p as int] < self.parent.len() 
    36	                   && self.rank[i as int] < self.rank[p as int] {
    37	                    self.spec_find(p as usize)
    38	                } else {
    39	                    i
    40	                }
    41	            } else {
    42	                i
    43	            }
    44	        }
    45	        // </preamble>
    46	
    47	        // Following is the block for potential helper specifications
    48	        // <helpers>
    49	        
    50	
    51	        // </helpers>
    52	
    53	        // Following is the block for proofs of lemmas
    54	        // <proofs>
    55	
    56	        // </proofs>
    57	
    58	        // Following is the block for the main specification
    59	        // <spec>
    60	        pub fn link_roots(&mut self, root_i: usize, root_j: usize)
    61	            requires
    62	                old(self).is_valid(),
    63	                root_i < old(self).parent.len(),
    64	                root_j < old(self).parent.len(),
    65	                old(self).parent[root_i as int] == root_i,
    66	                old(self).parent[root_j as int] == root_j,
    67	            ensures
    68	                self.is_valid(),
    69	                self.parent.len() == old(self).parent.len(),
    70	                // Functional Correctness:
    71	                // 1. root_i and root_j are now in the same set
    72	                self.spec_find(root_i) == self.spec_find(root_j),
    73	                // 2. The set structure is stable (only the merged roots changed)
    74	                // (Optional but good for completeness)
    75	                forall|k: usize| k != root_i && k != root_j && 0 <= k < self.parent.len() ==>
    76	                     old(self).parent[k as int] == k ==> self.parent[k as int] == k,
    77	        // </spec>
    78	        // <code>
    79	        {
    80	            // TODO: Implement the link root operation for union-find data structure here.
    81	        }
    82	        // </code>
    83	    }
    84	
    85	    fn main() {}
    86	
    87	}description.md
